This product includes software developed by Om AI Lab, published as OmDet
(https://github.com/om-ai-lab/OmDet), and described in "Real-time
Transformer-based Open-Vocabulary Detection with Efficient Fusion Head" (Zhao,
Liu, He, Zhang, Lee; arXiv:2403.06892).

The modules here are extracted from the PyTorch implementation published as
transformers/models/omdet_turbo (Copyright 2024 Om Research Lab and The
HuggingFace Inc. team), the hybrid encoder it copies from
transformers/models/rt_detr, the deformable attention it copies from
transformers/models/deformable_detr, and the Swin Transformer it runs from
timm/models/swin_transformer.py (Copyright 2021 Ross Wightman). All four are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see the LICENSE file in this
directory. The authors' own repository is Apache-2.0 as well.

Swin Transformer itself is Microsoft's:

  - Swin Transformer
    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
    https://github.com/microsoft/Swin-Transformer
    MIT License

The published checkpoint is Apache-2.0, as Om AI Lab states on its model card.

The byte-pair tokenizer and its vocabulary are OpenAI's:

  - CLIP
    Copyright (c) 2021 OpenAI
    https://github.com/openai/CLIP
    MIT License

  assets/bpe_simple_vocab_16e6.txt.gz is byte-identical to the file published
  there (sha256 924691ac288e54409236115652ad4aa250f48203de50a9e4722a6ecd48d6804a),
  and the vocabulary it builds is identical, id for id, to the vocab.json and
  merges.txt Om AI Lab publishes beside the checkpoint.

  assets/lowercase.json.gz is a table of Unicode lowercase mappings, derived from
  the Lowercase normaliser of Hugging Face's tokenizers (Apache-2.0) by
  tools/fetch/omdet_turbo.py.

NOT INCLUDED
